.TH LINELIGHT 1 "2026-10-31" "linelight 2026.10.32" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linelight \- add semantic colour to plain command output and logs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linelight filter
.B \-\-profile
.I ID
.RB [ \-\-color
.IR auto | always | never ]
.RB [ \-\-max-record
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-profile-dir
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-palette
.IR PATH ]
.br
.B linelight run
.B \-\-profile
.I ID
.RB [ \-\-color
.IR auto | always | never ]
.RB [ \-\-stderr ]
.RB [ \-\-pty ]
.B \-\-
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARG ...]
.br
.B linelight init
.I SHELL
.RB [ \-\-profile-dir
.IR DIR ]
.br
.B linelight profiles
.RB [ \-\-profile-dir
.IR DIR ]
.br
.B linelight explain
.B \-\-profile
.I ID
.RB [ \-\-profile-dir
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-palette
.IR PATH ]
.br
.B linelight check
.RI [ PATH ...]
.RB [ \-\-profile-dir
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-palette
.IR PATH ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B linelight
is a standalone, unprivileged filter and command runner. It adds semantic SGR
styles to plain UTF-8 records and preserves every other byte.
.PP
Profiles are explicit. The program does not wrap commands, rewrite argv,
change PATH, export colour environment variables, select replacement
utilities, or manage services.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B filter
Read stdin and write styled stdout. The default colour mode is
.BR auto :
colour only when stdout is a terminal and neither
.B NO_COLOR
(non-empty) nor
.B TERM=dumb
disables it. Explicit
.B always
and
.B never
win.
.TP
.B run
Run a command with stdout, and optionally stderr, filtered. The child keeps
the caller's stdin and foreground process group. With colour off, the command
is exec'd directly. Exit status is the child's, or 128+N when the child dies
from signal N.
.TP
.B init
Print shell wrappers for
.BR bash ,
.BR zsh ,
.BR tcsh ,
or
.BR fish .
Only commands with an effective profile and on PATH are wrapped; existing
aliases/functions win; `log` is never wrapped and `ls` is off by default.
.TP
.B profiles
List effective profile IDs, names, and sources.
.TP
.B explain
Show a profile's effective source, palette, rules, and styles.
.TP
.B check
Validate explicit profile paths, or every effective profile when no paths
are given.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-profile\  ID
Profile ID, or an explicit
.I .toml
file path.
.TP
.BI \-\-color\  MODE
.BR auto ,
.BR always ,
or
.BR never .
.TP
.BI \-\-max-record\  N
Bypass records longer than
.I N
bytes until the next LF. Default 65536.
.TP
.BI \-\-profile-dir\  DIR
Additional profile directory. Repeatable; earlier entries take precedence.
.TP
.BI \-\-palette\  PATH
Palette TOML file.
.TP
.B \-\-stderr
For
.BR run ,
filter stderr separately with its own destination-based colour decision.
.TP
.B \-\-pty
For
.BR run ,
give only stdout a pseudoterminal. stdin, stderr, and the controlling terminal
stay real. Cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-stderr .
.SH PROFILE RESOLUTION
Explicit file, then
.I ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/linelight/profiles
by stable ID, then each
.BR \-\-profile-dir ,
then embedded defaults. An override replaces a profile as a whole. There is no
system-wide or current-directory lookup.
.SH BYTE POLICY
Records containing ESC/ANSI, NUL, other control bytes, a lone carriage return,
or invalid UTF-8 pass through unchanged. LF, CRLF, and a final line without a
newline are preserved. Progress/control markers flush immediately. Removing
only inserted SGR sequences yields the original bytes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B filter
and management commands exit 0 on success, 1 on profile/config/output errors,
and 2 on usage errors.
.B run
returns the child's exit status, or 128+N when the child dies from signal N.
Command-not-found is 127; permission denied is 126.
.SH ADAPTER CONFIG
.B ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/linelight/adapters.toml
can disable individual generated wrappers:
.PP
.nf
schema = 1
disable = ["ps", "diff"]
.fi
.PP
Set
.B LINELIGHT_INIT=0
to make
.B init
print nothing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.I DESIGN.md
in the source distribution.
.SH AUTHOR
linelight contributors.
